  "narrative": {
    "intro": "National Steel and Shipbuilding shows $2.8B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding received 16 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $173M. National Steel and Shipbuilding obligations are up 404.3% year over year. Historical obligations show swings across recent years: FY21 $471M, FY22 $2.2B, FY23 $1.2B, FY24 $1.4B, and FY25 $550M. The FY2026 total is a partial fiscal-year figure and reflects current-year obligations to date. This profile highlights sudden growth in obligations for FY2026 to date compared with prior fiscal years, and a concentration in relatively large awards given the $173M average award size and the count of 16 awards. Use these figures when assessing contracting volume, award concentration, and year-over-year momentum for National Steel and Shipbuilding.",
